    "chart": {
      "$description": "Categorical data-series ramp (ADR-082). Unlike the hue ramps above this is a set of eight mutually-distinguishable series colours, not a lightness scale of one hue: 'light'/'dark' are the two authored themes (BR-BW-TOK-002), not scale steps. Hue is invariant per series across both themes because a series' identity is its hue; only lightness and chroma are authored per theme. Every value satisfies four properties verified in tests: an all-pairs separation floor of 0.12 in oklab, a minimum 28 degree hue separation, WCAG 1.4.11 3:1 against its own theme's surface, and hue stability across themes. See ADR-082 Decision 5.",
